-- Optional extraction, tuple input projection and deferred schema defaults retain
-- source references. Typing supplies their omission/shape/completeness facts;
-- no implicit tuple locals, renamed alias fields or HIR semantic payloads arise.
-- Explicit alias construction retains CallExpr SurfaceRef provenance and an
-- ordinary ResolvedReference role construction-target to its source alias.
-- Static application references remain ordinary bindings. Effective schema,
-- defaults and construction checking belong to typing; no callable or anchor
-- is created by this expression.
-- Comprehension iterator leaves are shared by sibling filter/result scopes.
-- Source and step use the outer scope; selector interpretation and coverage
-- are elaboration facts and create no nominal HIR type fields.
-- Canonical operator contract graphs and reflective operand records are typed
-- results specified separately; this nominal model adds no effective signature.
-- Operator metadata retains its source owner; typed signature anchors and reflective
-- operand contracts are not nominal HIR fields. Invocation operand bindings are
-- unavailable in the declaration metadata environment.
-- Alias operator declarations/operands retain SurfaceRef provenance.
-- Operator selection and signature-dependent public anchors belong to typing.
-- Preserve original alias ownership and separate declaration-local operand scopes;
-- no selected target, inferred type or type-dependent anchor is manufactured here.
-- Exact binding-pattern leaves use computed/stored/iterator LocalSymbol kinds.
-- Ordinals follow textual depth-first leaf order; discards create no symbol or edge.
-- Type holes have SurfaceRef provenance only, no symbol, inferred type or HIR payload.
-- File/part catalogues enforce part-only and direct uses before lookup.
-- Normal/sub operations create their own nominal categories and anchors.
-- Part headers and uses declarations create no symbols, owners or anchors;
-- no visibility, callable-capability or contract-type proof is stored here.
-- Generic parameters use LocalSymbol kind type-parameter in a joint header/body scope.
-- Application constructors/arguments keep SurfaceRef provenance and ordinary bindings.
-- Applications create no symbols or anchors. Specializes retains source constructors;
-- effective application ancestry, inferred arguments and closure proofs are elaboration.
-- PendingReceiverCall also defers static written-given compatibility, without storing it.

-- Functional parameters and cumulative input use LocalSymbol kinds
-- functional-parameter and functional-input. Source-ordered inferred binders
-- are created only for unresolved free lowerCamel references in an eligible
-- immutable functional definition; property labels and foreign tokens are not
-- references. Captures retain ordinary ResolvedReference edges to outer symbols.
-- Trait declarations have category trait and ordinary anchored ownership;
-- structural satisfaction never creates a Specializes edge.
-- Operator-reference families retain accessible nominal candidates using
-- PendingReceiverCall with role operator-family; typing resolves correlated
-- signatures, global collisions and instantiations outside this HIR.
-- No quantified scheme, runtime dispatch or selected type is stored here.
-- Refutable branch patterns use LocalSymbol kind selector-capture for first
-- textual depth-first captures. Repeated occurrences are ResolvedReference
-- role pattern-equality to that local, not fresh bindings or implicit parameters.
-- Type/field occurrences retain SurfaceRef provenance; match success, equality,
-- order proofs and capture contract joins remain outside nominal HIR.

module MUDNominalHIR {
    -- Arrow-owned specifications retain SurfaceRef provenance only. Their
    -- association counts, policy mode and result guarantees are typed facts;
    -- they create no symbols/scopes or effective-contract HIR payloads.
    source_span = SourceSpan(string file, int start_byte, int end_byte)
    anchor = Anchor(string value)
    scope_id = ScopeId(int value)

    -- Handler captures use LocalSymbol kind error-binding and clause-local scopes.
    -- Error typing and pending occurrence matching belong to later phases.
    symbol_id = AnchoredSymbol(anchor value)
              | LocalSymbol(anchor owner, string kind, string name, int ordinal)

    surface_ref = SurfaceRef(source_span origin, string role)

    nominal_project = NominalHIR(nominal_symbol* symbols,
                                 nominal_scope* scopes,
                                 nominal_reference* bindings,
                                 nominal_edge* edges)

    nominal_symbol = NominalSymbol(symbol_id identity,
                                   symbol_id? owner,
                                   string category,
                                   string source_name,
                                   scope_id scope,
                                   surface_ref declaration)

    nominal_scope = NominalScope(scope_id identity,
                                 scope_id? parent,
                                 symbol_id? owner,
                                 scope_entry* entries)

    scope_entry = ScopeEntry(string name, symbol_id symbol)

    lookup_level = LexicalLevel | OwnerLevel | CurrentPathLevel
                 | ExactUsingLevel | RecursiveUsingLevel | BuiltinLevel

    nominal_reference = ResolvedReference(surface_ref occurrence,
                                         symbol_id target,
                                         string role)
                      | PendingReceiverCall(surface_ref occurrence,
                                             symbol_id* candidates,
                                             lookup_level level,
                                             string role)

    nominal_edge = Owns(symbol_id owner, symbol_id member)
                 | Specializes(symbol_id derived, symbol_id base)
                 | RefersTo(symbol_id source, symbol_id target)
}
